  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Key Features**\n\nI\'m zeroing in on defining the essential features that elevate this contact directory app. The goal is to ensure it\'s not just functional, but exceptional and fully compliant with the user\'s requirements. Currently, my primary focus is the standalone HTML exporter, a critical element as it directly addresses two primary user demands, namely that it is a *standalone* file.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Feature Focus**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress by homing in on the `.html` export feature. This is now fully specified: a self-contained HTML file embedding all required data and functionality. It contains Tailwind CSS, icons, and contact data as an embedded JSON string. Pure vanilla JavaScript ensures full interactivity offline, addressing the user\'s need for a standalone, double-clickable file usable on any network drive. I\'ve also begun to define the data structure.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structure**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the data structure, defining key contact fields. Each contact entry will include first name, last name, position, department, landline, mobile, email, office room, notes, and a \"favorites\" toggle. I want to include all important fields for easy contact management and quick access. I\'m also planning the user interface, aiming for a modern German administrative design, focusing on clarity, accessibility, and intuitive use. A header will show key stats and quick actions.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI refinements for the contact directory. I\'m prioritizing implementing live search across key fields and introducing filtering options for location, department, and favorites. I will focus on view switcher options: Tabellenansicht for desktop, Kartenansicht for responsiveness, and Gruppierte Ansicht for organization. Finally, a modal editor for contact creation, editing and deletion is planned.\n\n\n**Adding Interactive Features**\n\nI am now focusing on interactive additions for the user. I\'m adding one-click copy and action buttons. Instant feedback confirms when a phone number or email is copied to the clipboard. \"tel:\" and \"mailto:\" links will initiate calls and emails directly, respectively. I\'m also planning a QR code generator for easy mobile contact import, all in vCard format. Moreover, there is a print mode for a clean black-and-white table view, optimized via CSS. Finally, I\'ll add initial realistic sample data.\n\n\n**Implementing Export Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the export logic, ensuring that the entire application state, including contacts, filters, and UI settings, is bundled into a single HTML string. This exported HTML file will embed HTML, Tailwind CSS, and vanilla JavaScript to ensure local storage sync, searching, filtering, contact management, JSON import/export, and printing. The user will obtain a `Telefonverzeichnis.html` file by clicking the \"Als Standalone .html exportieren\" button, ready for immediate use and distribution. I am also working on the folder structure.\n\n\n**Structuring Project Modules**\n\nI\'m now making steady progress on structuring the project modules. I\'m focusing on defining core components for the user interface. I\'m actively establishing the directory `/src/components` with files for each view and interaction. Currently, I\'m working on defining `ContactCard.tsx`, `ContactGrid.tsx`, `ContactGrouped.tsx`, `ContactModal.tsx`, `ImportExportModal.tsx`, `VCardModal.tsx`, and `DeleteConfirmModal.tsx`. I will be creating a function in `/src/lib/standaloneHtmlGenerator.ts` to bundle the entire application. Moreover, I\'ll be creating `/src/types.ts`. I also made sure that lucide-react is installed!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 278461233
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
