xtracting the last set of contacts, focusing specifically on those from Saarbr\303\274cken and Stuttgart, including all final details. I\'m meticulously recording each name, role, department, and all associated contact details, including phone numbers and emails. I will now ensure that I\'ve captured every single datum correctly.\n\n\n**Completing The Extraction**\n\nI\'m now extracting the last contacts from the document. This includes final contacts from Stuttgart, as well as Magdeburg and the Pumpenabteilung. I\'m focusing on ensuring accuracy with the latest contact details from the provided data. I\'ve recorded the names, job titles, and contact information.\n\n\n**Finalizing Last Entries**\n\nI\'m now extracting the last set of contacts, focusing specifically on those from the Pumpenabteilung and the Elektroabteilung. I\'m carefully recording each name, role, department, and all associated contact details. I am meticulously recording these final data, including the Pumpenabteilung contacts like Kuschkowitz Kai and Kr\303\274ger Andy. Next, I am capturing the Elektroabteilung contacts, starting with Bayer Tim.\n\n\n**Finalizing Data Capture**\n\nI\'m now extracting the last set of contacts: the Elektroabteilung, HDWN, and MONTAGEMEISTER groups. I\'m meticulously recording each name, role, department, phone numbers, and emails. Specifically, I\'m logging entries from the final data set including Jokar Abdul Hossein and Neumann Mirko. I am ensuring data integrity.\n\n\n**Designing Master Data Storage**\n\nI\'m now shifting focus to designing the master data storage system. I\'m going to create `src/lib/masterDataStorage.ts` to manage `Standorte` and `Abteilungen` centrally. I plan to use `localStorage` for data persistence. This system aims to ensure data quality by allowing the user to select predefined values for locations and departments when adding contacts.\n\n\n**Designing Data Storage**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing a more robust data storage system in