  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Master Data Logic**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on adding master data management logic. I\'m starting by integrating the provided `jsonContacts` and `jsonStandorte` data into the script. I\'ll modify the `standaloneHtmlGenerator.ts` file directly, focusing on how these initial datasets will be structured and used within the HTML generation process. The aim is to create a robust data layer for master data.\n\n\n**Defining Storage Keys**\n\nI\'ve defined several storage keys to manage persistent data. Specifically, I have keys for contacts, master standorte, and abteilungen. The get/save functions are now defined for contacts, and I\'m adding functions to handle master standorte. The storage is used to persist data in the browser. I\'m focusing on handling data persistence across sessions.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Persistence**\n\nI\'ve just implemented data persistence for master standorte and abteilungen, adding `getMasterStandorte`, `saveMasterStandorte`, `getMasterAbteilungen`, and `saveMasterAbteilungen` functions. These utilize `localStorage` to store and retrieve data. I\'ve also integrated the new persistence functions by calling `updateLocationSelect()`. I\'m verifying the data\'s persistence behavior across sessions.\n\n\n**Refining Data Display**\n\nI\'m now refining how location and department data is displayed. I\'ve integrated `getMasterStandorte` and `getMasterAbteilungen` to populate location and department lists. I\'m dynamically generating select options and datalist options from combined sets of master data and contact data to ensure comprehensive lists. I\'m focusing on preserving the currently selected location. I\'m also ensuring the datalist is updated correctly.\n\n\n**Managing Master Modal Actions**\n\nI\'m working on the master modal now. I\'ve defined `openMasterModal`, `closeMasterModal`, and `switchMasterTab` functions for handling the modal\'s lifecycle and tab switching. The modal updates when opened, cleared inputs, and re-renders lists. I\'m also implementing the update of tab button counters based on stored master data.\n\n\n**Refining Tab Selection**\n\nI\'m now refining the tab selection within the master modal. I\'ve updated the logic to dynamically manage the styling and class names of the tab buttons, ensuring that the active tab is visually distinguished from inactive ones. I\'m focusing on providing clear visual feedback to the user regarding the currently selected tab.\n\n\n**Implementing Master List Filtering**\n\nI\'m implementing filtering for the master lists now. I\'ve integrated a filtering mechanism that searches and displays matching entries within the master lists. If no items match, the container displays a \"No entries found\" message. Furthermore, I\'ve added inline editing, allowing users to modify list items directly within the displayed list.\n\n\n**Enhancing List Display**\n\nI\'ve just added inline editing functionality to the master lists, along with delete buttons to match the example. I\'m dynamically generating list items with edit and delete options, and the edit is calling the appropriate javascript function. If an item exists, the delete button is rendered. No, I\'m verifying the new UI components and interaction patterns.\n\n\n**Refining Item Management**\n\nI\'m now refining item management within master lists, specifically for standorte and abteilungen. I\'ve implemented logic to add new items, ensuring they don\'t already exist and are properly sorted. I\'ve added functions to start, cancel, and save edits to items. I\'m focusing on seamless update of the UI to reflect changes and clearing the input afterwards.\n\n\n**Updating Data Associations**\n\nI\'ve just implemented the renaming and deletion logic for master list items. When a standort or abteilung is renamed, I\'m updating corresponding entries in the contacts data to ensure consistency. Likewise, the delete function removes items from the master data. I\'m taking care to show confirmation dialogs and re-render the lists after any change. I\'m verifying the data integrity of all relationships after any change.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 878658599
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
