  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Feature Set**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the React app\'s features in detail, specifically contrasting them with the requirements for the `generateStandaloneHtml()` function. The header elements are my current focus, noting the title, subtitle, and the various statistic badges that need replication.\n\n\n**Detailing Interaction Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interaction elements within the application. I\'ve broken down the available action buttons, noting their functionality; \"Neuer Kontakt\", \"Stammdaten verwalten\", \"JSON Import/Export\", \"Drucken\", and \"PDF-Reset\". I am also investigating the search and filter options. I\'m noting the live search input, Standort and Abteilung dropdown filters. I\'m particularly interested in the `table`, `cards`, and `grouped` views, with attention on clickable headers, badges, and their associated actions.\n\n\n**Examining Advanced Filters**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the advanced filtering options. I\'ve taken note of the Quick Pill Filter Bar, which includes \"Alle\" and individual \"Standort\" pills. Also the Favorites filter toggle, and the Alphabet Quick Jumper Bar, which allows quickly filtering with letter buttons with contact counts. Finally, the counter and reset filter button is also in my sights.\n\n\n**Defining Data Operations**\n\nI\'m now outlining data import/export functionalities. This includes downloading the database as `telefonverzeichnis_kontakte.json`, and uploading JSON files with overwrite and merge options. I\'ve also added the ability to copy JSON data to the clipboard. I am starting to check for needed helpers and libraries and also checking FontAwesome 6.4.0.\n\n\n**Constructing Standalone Version**\n\nI\'m now focused on the standalone HTML structure.  I\'ve confirmed the Font Awesome and Tailwind CDNs are present. My primary task is replicating the React app\'s functionality precisely, including the JavaScript state management. I\'m noting the state variables required, like `viewMode`, `sortField`, `sortOrder`, `searchQuery`, and the initial data arrays. I\'m focusing on the necessary data import/export functions.\n\n\n**Defining State and Helpers**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the state variables: `Standort`, `selectedAbteilung`, `alphabetFilter`, `onlyFavorites`, `collapsedGroups`, `vCardContactId`, `deleteContactId`, `importMode`, `masterActiveTab`, and `editingMasterItem`. I\'ve outlined helper functions in JavaScript. These include `getContacts()`, `saveContacts()`, and the master data functions, plus `toggleFavorite()` and initial `generateVCardString()`.\n\n\n**Implementing VCard Functions**\n\nI\'ve just added the crucial vCard functionality. The focus is now on generating the vCard string for each contact, constructing QR code URLs, and enabling download/copy actions. I have created `openVCardModal()`, `downloadVCardFile()`, and `copyVCardText()` methods for improved interaction. I am also implementing modals for delete and import/export, complete with confirmations and file handling.\n\n\n**Rendering Contact Displays**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the contacts will be displayed, implementing the dynamic rendering logic. I\'ve successfully mapped the filtering and sorting processes to ensure data integrity and user interaction. The script now updates the quick pill bar with counts per Standort. It also handles A-Z alphabet bar updates, which will include active letter styling and count badges. Finally, I\'m working to render contacts based on the view mode, whether it\'s the `table`, `cards`, or `grouped` view. This will render the headers with clickable sort controls.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 85
      nanos: 357449507
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
