  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Server Architecture**\n\nI\'m now laying out the initial steps, starting with the creation of `server.ts`. This involves constructing an Express server to handle API endpoints. The first endpoint, `GET /api/contacts`, will retrieve contact data from `data/contacts.json`, initializing the file if it\'s missing.\n\n\n**Outlining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve specified the API endpoints. I am now finalizing the details for `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, and `DELETE` requests for both contacts and master data. I\'m also including a reset endpoint and an import feature. Static file serving and Vite dev middleware considerations are now in progress. Port 3000 will be used.\n\n\n**Implementing API Communication**\n\nI am now focusing on the client-side API service. I\'m building `src/lib/api.ts`, which includes auto-sync, polling, and error handling. I\'ve designed functions to communicate with the backend\'s `/api/*` endpoints for contacts and master data, and also for a reset function. I will be updating `src/App.tsx` next to integrate this API layer.\n\n\n**Constructing Dockerization**\n\nI\'m now detailing the Docker setup. I\'m writing a `Dockerfile` for a two-stage build, using `node:20-alpine`, and creating a `docker-compose.yml` to define the service, ports (3000), volume mounts (`./data:/app/data`), and restart policies. I\'m also preparing a `.dockerignore` file and will write detailed German documentation for Portainer deployment and general usage.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 254891986
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
